# Pocket Node Rules

- Treat this repo as an Android/Kotlin app with a single Gradle module: `:app`.
- The application id is `com.pocketnode.app`. Keep that stable unless the user explicitly requests an app id migration.
- Preserve the offline-first design. Do not introduce cloud services, hosted APIs, analytics SDKs, telemetry, or other network dependencies unless the user explicitly asks.
- Prefer local/on-device implementation paths:
  - UI is Jetpack Compose.
  - Persistence is Room/DataStore.
  - Background and async work uses Kotlin coroutines and Flow.
  - Local inference lives in `com.pocketnode.app.inference` and native C++ under `app/src/main/cpp`.
- Do not edit Kotlin source files unless the user explicitly asks for code changes in those files.
- If you need to document behavior, prefer repo docs over code comments.
- Keep build, install, and test instructions aligned with Gradle and adb on Windows.
- When adding new files, keep them consistent with the existing package structure and naming conventions.
- Avoid adding dependencies that require cloud credentials, external services, or remote execution.
- If a task can be completed by editing docs or build metadata, do that instead of changing application logic.

